Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:19.317
How a Kar98k Works

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:28.160
Lifting the bolt forces the 'cocking piece'&nbsp;
to the rear, partially cocking the action.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.280
The cocking piece rides along a&nbsp;
ramp in the bolt, forcing it back.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.440
A cross section shows the compression of&nbsp;
the 'firing pin spring' when lifting the bolt.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.887
The bolt is pulled to the rear to load&nbsp;
the ammunition.

00:00:45.448 --> 00:00:50.153
Cartridges can be loaded&nbsp;individually
or five at a time using a stripper&nbsp;clip.

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:53.908
The clip is ejected when the bolt is closed.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.738
Pressing the bolt forward strips the top cartridge,&nbsp;

00:00:58.738 --> 00:01:02.594
which is directed into the chamber 
under the&nbsp;control of the extractor.

00:01:03.545 --> 00:01:07.619
Closing the bolt locks&nbsp;the two front 
locking lugs into the receiver.

00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:15.305
The 'sear' keeps the cocking piece held back as&nbsp;
the bolt is closed, fully cocking the action.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.449
The Kar98k is equipped with a 'two-stage trigger'.

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:25.530
Initial trigger pull provides resistance
and&nbsp;slightly lowers the sear.

00:01:26.063 --> 00:01:31.593
This feature cues the&nbsp;shooter to imminent firing
and permits a crisper release of the striker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.177 --> 00:01:38.000
Continued trigger pull&nbsp;engages the second lobe
of the trigger, fully&nbsp;disengaging the sear.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.269
This releases the firing&nbsp;
pin, causing it to strike the cartridge primer.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.559
The expanding gases from the powder&nbsp;
charge propel the bullet through the barrel.

00:01:54.432 --> 00:01:58.156
The 'extractor' grips the rim of the spent&nbsp;
cartridge case.

00:01:58.806 --> 00:02:03.323
Lifting and pulling back the bolt
extracts the case from the chamber. 

00:02:04.927 --> 00:02:10.971
As the bolt&nbsp;travels to the rear, a spring inside the bolt stop pushes the 'ejector' inward,

00:02:10.971 --> 00:02:14.277
forcing the&nbsp;case out of the rifle as it makes contact.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:21.840
The 'bolt stop' engages the left bolt lug, preventing&nbsp;
it from coming out of the rifle upon extraction.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.058
Pulling outward on the bolt stop, allows the&nbsp;
bolt to be removed for cleaning and maintenance.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.085
The Kar98k uses a 'safety' to prevent the rifle&nbsp;from firing.

00:02:34.715 --> 00:02:38.959
In the left position, the safety is&nbsp;off to fully permit firing.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.640
In the up position, the striker is 
prevented from moving forward.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.328
The bolt however can still be opened and removed.&nbsp;

00:02:48.176 --> 00:02:54.466
In the right position, an extension of the safety
fits into a notch on the bolt, locking it closed.

00:02:55.422 --> 00:02:58.247
The striker remains blocked in this position.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.702
Housed within the bolt sleeve, is a 'lock plunger'.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:10.080
As the bolt is opened and pulled to the rear, 
the plunger engages the safety notch on the bolt,

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.094
preventing the bolt sleeve from&nbsp;
rotating during manipulation.

